## How to Make the Most of Your Family Trip

| Category | Recommendation |
|----------|----------------|
| **Transport** | Use the **Milan City Pass** (family‑friendly) for unlimited metro, tram, and bus rides plus discounts on entry fees. |
| **Tickets** | Book online for the Duomo rooftop and the guided tour to avoid long queues. |
| **Meals** | Look for restaurants with kids’ menus; many cafés in the Galleria and Brera offer pizza, pasta, and gelato. |
| **Rest Breaks** | Plan a midday break at **Parco Sempione** (great playground, open‑air cinema in summer) or a café in the Galleria. |
| **Safety** | Keep an eye on belongings in crowded spots; use a child‑friendly backpack with a lock. |
| **Apps** | Download the “Cathedral Quest” app before you go – it turns the Duomo visit into a game with virtual stickers and fun facts. |

---

### Sample 2‑Day Itinerary (Family‑Friendly)

| Day | Morning | Lunch | Afternoon | Evening |
|-----|---------|-------|-----------|---------|
| **Day 1** | Duomo di Milano (rooftop) | Panini at Galleria Vittorio Emanuele II | Guided Duomo tour | Gelato at Galleria |
| **Day 2** | Milano Design Tour | Pizza at a family‑friendly trattoria | Discover the Milano by Food (kids’ cooking demo) | Sunset walk along the Navigli canals (great photo ops) |

Feel free to swap attractions or add extra stops (e.g., Sforza Castle, Brera Art Gallery) based on your family’s interests. Enjoy your trip to Milan!

